# state: any   (golden 9153c63300da; lane.savestate433 -- same golden as routes/gta-3.route)
# Grand Theft Auto III (5454000E): the classifier-driven path to play, on top of
# drive-profiles/gta3.toml's letterbox-top/hud-heart crops (#433, lane.localdrive1018 Part D).
#
# STAGE 1 of this file's eventual plan, named honestly: only this one step has run against
# a live device so far. It replaces gta-3.route's hand-timed, fixed-wait A-trains with
# drive.py's screen-aware loop (classify.py + gta3.toml), so a boot that runs faster or
# slower than any one run -- the exact failure gtawedge1012 hit on gta-3.route itself, see
# that file's own header -- no longer needs a new hand-tuned wait per run. `find`: end the
# step at 20 s of confirmed play (nothing scored yet); the frames and route-solution.json
# this step produces are the live evidence Part D's remaining pieces (a car-entry crop, the
# pause-menu Save-row crop, the held-out false-gameplay number) need and did not have before
# this run -- see docs/lanes/localdrive1018/NOTES.md "Part D".
#
# STAGE 2 (added 2026-10-19, off a separate probe run -- see below): car entry. `Y` is not
# gated behind `drive`/the profile-gate check (no `drive` step touches it), so this much was
# dispatchable and run pre-merge via a standalone probe route
# (routes/gta3-car-pause-probe.route, result 1-1792380791-localdrive1018-729348, nova,
# 2026-10-19): Y, from on-foot next to the car, puts the player in the driver's seat within
# one capture. `car-entered` below is a real reference crop (the "Kuruma" vehicle-nameplate
# watermark GTA III draws briefly over the car after entry), built from that run's own
# `car-entered.png` frame and scored with waitfor_match.py's own scoring function against
# every other frame that run captured: 0.0 on itself, 17.2-17.4 on the on-foot/pregameplay
# frames, 31.1-31.7 on the pause-menu/resumed frames, 44.6 on the cutscene frame -- comfortably
# separated at threshold 10.0. Caveats, stated plainly: this is ONE sample (no second car-entry
# capture exists to confirm the margin generalizes), the watermark names this specific vehicle
# ("Kuruma") so a run where a different car spawns at this spot may not match at all, and the
# region (780,740,400,90, raw pixel coords) was measured on a Nova (1280x960) capture only --
# unverified on the Thor's different pillarboxed geometry, same open caveat `fist-hud` already
# carries from gta-3.route. Full numbers and the frames themselves:
# docs/lanes/localdrive1018/gta3-car-pause-probe-1019/, NOTES.md "Resume 2026-10-19".
#
# NOT YET HERE: the state-save step and the drive loop itself. The save step is blocked on
# more than a device now -- the same probe run found the pause menu's default tab shows
# "New Game"/"Load Game", not a Save row, at this spawn point (GTA III saves only at a
# safehouse); see routes/gta3-car-pause-probe.route's own RESULT note and NOTES.md for the
# correction to the brief's "Save is the default row" premise. Driving to a safehouse first,
# or the owner naming where Save actually shows from here, is needed before this step can be
# built, not just a device slot.
drive gta3 300 find
wait 1
press Y 300
wait 3
waitfor car-entered 10 780,740,400,90 10
